  "interpretation": {
    "main_obstruction": "The current n-window cannot rule out flexible zero-limit curves. A finite-data claim must pre-register a zero-limit family or bring in theory that lower-bounds the decay exponent.",
    "decisive_pattern_for_persistence": "Later windows keep Delta_n and the Jensen component positive while the best zero-limit models become AICc-worse across independent eval roots.",
